WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.365 --> 00:00:15.249
"You!" Zann blurted out in surprise.

2
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.770
His voice was louder than he'd intended.

3
00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:21.472
He glanced nervously at the door, expecting Slib to burst in.

4
00:00:21.492 --> 00:00:25.213
"Don't worry, Zann, he can't hear you."

5
00:00:25.654 --> 00:00:27.635
The old woman dropped the bag she was holding.

6
00:00:27.655 --> 00:00:30.836
"This room is hidden from most people."

7
00:00:32.008 --> 00:00:33.509
"How do you know my name?"

8
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:34.670
Zann demanded.

9
00:00:35.371 --> 00:00:39.314
Then he realized he knew hers too—at least he thought he did.

10
00:00:40.015 --> 00:00:41.176
Teplo had mentioned it once.

11
00:00:41.196 --> 00:00:43.397
"You're Wyssa, aren't you?"

12
00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:47.161
"That's what they call me, yes," Wyssa said.

13
00:00:47.181 --> 00:00:52.185
"Now take my hand, and I'll zap you out of the palace before you're noticed."

14
00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:54.306
"No!" Zann said.

15
00:00:54.647 --> 00:00:58.690
"Not until you tell me everything you know about how my parents disappeared!"

16
00:00:59.791 --> 00:01:00.892
Wyssa looked startled.

17
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:01.868
"How did you—?

18
00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.449
Never mind," she interrupted herself.

19
00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:09.651
"I suppose the old man told you I was involved."

20
00:01:09.671 --> 00:01:12.972
"Huh?" Now it was Zann's turn to be startled.

21
00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:14.472
"What old man?

22
00:01:14.832 --> 00:01:17.033
Wait—are you talking about Boz?"

23
00:01:17.793 --> 00:01:18.473
"Who else?"

24
00:01:18.913 --> 00:01:19.574
Wyssa sighed.

25
00:01:19.594 --> 00:01:22.494
"He's been poking around these past few years.

26
00:01:23.435 --> 00:01:24.895
I know he must suspect me."

27
00:01:26.036 --> 00:01:27.316
Zann didn't know what to say.

28
00:01:28.096 --> 00:01:31.637
All this time he'd thought Boz was doing nothing to find Zann's parents.

29
00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:35.998
"I suppose you deserve to know what happened," Wyssa said.

30
00:01:36.018 --> 00:01:38.099
"It doesn't matter now anyway.

31
00:01:39.019 --> 00:01:44.541
It all began when a very demanding new customer sent me to pick up a scatter beast in

32
00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.861
Fardark." "Fardark?"

33
00:01:47.242 --> 00:01:47.722
Zann said.

34
00:01:48.382 --> 00:01:53.183
The name sounded vaguely familiar, though for a moment he couldn't remember where he'd heard it.

35
00:01:54.024 --> 00:01:55.064
Then it came back to him.

36
00:01:55.796 --> 00:01:59.500
He'd seen it in Boz's diary while he was reading about his parents' travels.

37
00:02:00.281 --> 00:02:02.483
Fardark was the name of another world!

38
00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:06.507
"It should have been an ordinary errand," Wyssa went on.

39
00:02:06.527 --> 00:02:14.976
"But my customer insisted I return via a wormhole that was convenient for him—one near the university.

40
00:02:15.837 --> 00:02:18.880
Your parents happened to be entering at the same moment.

41
00:02:19.712 --> 00:02:25.716
The chaotic energy of the scatter beast turned what should have been a minor collision into an explosion

42
00:02:25.756 --> 00:02:27.077
of unstable magic.

43
00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:30.639
I tried to grab your parents, to pull them out with me.

44
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.781
But I wasn't able to save them.

45
00:02:32.941 --> 00:02:36.503
They went spinning off course and became stuck between worlds."

46
00:02:37.384 --> 00:02:39.305
Once again Zann was speechless.

47
00:02:40.006 --> 00:02:41.707
His mind buzzed with questions.

48
00:02:42.827 --> 00:02:47.390
But before he could ask any of them, a zap of energy shot through the room, and Morb

49
00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.472
appeared. "There you are!"

50
00:02:49.856 --> 00:02:51.837
he said irritably, glaring at Wyssa.

51
00:02:51.857 --> 00:02:55.000
"What in the world are you doing in here?

52
00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.663
I don't like having to track you when I—" Morb stopped short as he noticed Zann.

53
00:03:01.424 --> 00:03:03.345
His eyes widened.

54
00:03:03.365 --> 00:03:04.926
"You!" he spat out.

55
00:03:04.946 --> 00:03:08.549
"Where are they taking us?"

56
00:03:09.009 --> 00:03:09.709
Gliss whispered.

57
00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.451
They had walked deep into the forest.

58
00:03:13.072 --> 00:03:15.113
Perda shrugged, glancing at their captors.

59
00:03:15.754 --> 00:03:19.096
There were about half a dozen of them, all with stern looks on their faces.

60
00:03:19.952 --> 00:03:22.074
None of them would tell Fala or the kids anything.

61
00:03:22.775 --> 00:03:25.477
Perda had been ready to fight back against that Floating spell.

62
00:03:26.077 --> 00:03:29.781
But then she, Gliss, and Fala had Restrain spells placed on them.

63
00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:34.144
Perda looked down at her arms, which appeared to be stuck at her sides.

64
00:03:35.486 --> 00:03:36.526
They came to a clearing.

65
00:03:36.887 --> 00:03:38.748
Several dozen people were gathered there.

66
00:03:39.509 --> 00:03:41.731
As Fala looked around, her eyes lit up.

67
00:03:41.751 --> 00:03:43.933
"Shem!" she called.

68
00:03:44.273 --> 00:03:45.214
A man turned around.

69
00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:47.156
"Fala?" he exclaimed.

70
00:03:48.924 --> 00:03:50.565
"I can't believe you're here."

71
00:03:50.585 --> 00:03:53.905
"Well, you have these people to thank for it."

72
00:03:54.646 --> 00:03:56.126
Fala nodded toward the captors.

73
00:03:56.146 --> 00:03:58.327
"They grabbed us in the forest."

74
00:03:59.387 --> 00:03:59.967
Shem laughed.

75
00:04:01.728 --> 00:04:05.229
"You can remove the Restrain spells," he told the captors.

76
00:04:06.049 --> 00:04:07.349
"They're on our side."

77
00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.830
Perda shook her arms.

78
00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.551
"Who are these people?"

79
00:04:12.911 --> 00:04:13.731
she asked Fala.

80
00:04:13.751 --> 00:04:15.772
"Don't worry," Fala said.

81
00:04:16.432 --> 00:04:17.152
"They're friends."

82
00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:21.883
Shem told Fala that he and his group had been among the people who'd marched on the palace

83
00:04:21.903 --> 00:04:22.443
that morning.

84
00:04:23.604 --> 00:04:28.007
Now they were hiding in the woods, trying to figure out how to fight back against Morb.

85
00:04:28.027 --> 00:04:31.209
"Fala can help us," Shem told the group.

86
00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:35.192
"She has powerful friends and much knowledge."

87
00:04:36.052 --> 00:04:39.755
As the adults started discussing possible plans, Perda stopped listening.

88
00:04:39.775 --> 00:04:44.418
"I thought Zann would have found us by now," she whispered to Gliss and Darb.

89
00:04:44.438 --> 00:04:46.439
"I hope he's okay."

90
00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:53.301
Zann stared at Morb, gripped by the fury and triumph in the evil man's eyes.

91
00:04:54.142 --> 00:04:59.163
As Morb touched his fingertips together and sparks flew, Zann quickly rubbed his hands together.

92
00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:01.164
"Zap!" he cried.

93
00:05:01.564 --> 00:05:02.204
Nothing happened.

94
00:05:02.224 --> 00:05:05.425
"Too late, boy," sneered Morb.

95
00:05:05.445 --> 00:05:10.246
"Even a clever Red like you can't fight a Dousing spell."

96
00:05:14.528 --> 00:05:15.828
Zann darted toward the exit.

97
00:05:16.556 --> 00:05:20.579
But at that moment, a troll stepped forward, blocking the doorway with its huge body.

98
00:05:21.499 --> 00:05:22.460
"Let me through!"

99
00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.782
Zann yelled, throwing himself at the troll.

100
00:05:24.802 --> 00:05:29.025
The troll grunted with surprise as Zann pounded on it with his fists.

101
00:05:29.625 --> 00:05:31.666
Then Zann saw a glint of silver.

102
00:05:32.347 --> 00:05:33.147
The talisman!

103
00:05:33.528 --> 00:05:38.651
He remembered Fala's words: If only we could get our hands on one of those talismans.

104
00:05:39.432 --> 00:05:40.913
It could be invaluable to us.

105
00:05:41.793 --> 00:05:44.155
Zann quickly grabbed the talisman and yanked it loose.

106
00:05:44.175 --> 00:05:45.716
"Get him!"

107
00:05:46.088 --> 00:05:46.648
Morb yelled.

108
00:05:47.009 --> 00:05:48.129
The troll reached down.

109
00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.832
Zann barely managed to slip free of the creature's grasp.

110
00:05:52.572 --> 00:05:55.854
He stuck the talisman in his pocket and ran to the middle of the room.

111
00:05:55.874 --> 00:06:00.237
"There's nowhere to run, boy!"

112
00:06:00.957 --> 00:06:02.198
Morb laughed nastily.

113
00:06:03.058 --> 00:06:06.641
Zann was desperately trying to think of a plan when Wyssa stepped toward him.

114
00:06:06.661 --> 00:06:09.923
"Take my hand, Zann," she said.

115
00:06:09.943 --> 00:06:11.944
"What?" he blurted out.

116
00:06:13.056 --> 00:06:15.698
Wyssa grabbed Zann's hand and yanked him toward the corner.

117
00:06:16.459 --> 00:06:18.080
Morb watched her suspiciously.

118
00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:24.864
"What are you—" A thunderous humming sound drowned out Morb's voice, and a glowing ring of light appeared

119
00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:25.305
in the room.

120
00:06:26.145 --> 00:06:30.188
As Zann peered into the swirling vortex, he nearly lost his balance.

121
00:06:30.208 --> 00:06:35.372
"Whatever you do, don't let go of my hand," warned Wyssa.

122
00:06:36.112 --> 00:06:38.814
With that, she pulled Zann into the wormhole.
